00:02:06.902 --> 00:02:14.480
&gt;&gt; This is a film about Leo Tolstoy's
brilliant novel War and Peace.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:18.790
War and Peace is a truly magnificent
literary achievement.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:27.260
It is also an extended essay, and the role
of leadership, in history.

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:31.590
The war of War and Peace was a conflict
between Russia and

00:02:31.590 --> 00:02:36.420
France, culminating in the French invasion
of Russia in 1812.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:40.940
The climactic battle of that

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:45.760
war was fought here at Borodino, not far
from Moscow.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:51.209
By night fall on September 7th,

00:02:51.209 --> 00:02:56.292
1812, some 40,000 French soldiers and

00:02:56.292 --> 00:03:03.400
some 45,000 Russian soldiers lay dead or
wounded on this field.

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:07.900
They are memorialized by this monument.

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:15.970
This is not however, a film about French
history, or

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:20.560
about Russian history, it is a film about
leaders.

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:29.181
War and Peace argues the stories of heroic
leaders creating history are myths.

00:03:29.181 --> 00:03:39.181
[MUSIC]

00:03:45.336 --> 00:03:51.776
